  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Program to scale up interventions in order to contribute to the reduction of TB related morbidity and mortality by - Cameroon (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cameroon, Tuberculosis, Ministry of Public Health of the Republic of Cameroon (MOH)This program has the following goals: Contribute to reducing TB-related morbidity and mortality by 2025. The objectives of this program are: Achieve 100 percent completeness and promptness of expected reports from TB programs and carry out at least 90 percent of planned supervisions in 2019.  Improve program and grant management capacity so as to increase the budget implementation rate to more than 90 percent in 2019.  Increase the number of tested MDR-TB patients undergoing treatment to 100 percent by 2019.  Increase the rate of HIV testing among notified TB patients from 87 percent in 2014 to 95 percent in 2019.  Increase the therapeutic success rate from 82 percent in 2013 to 87 percent in 2019.  Raise the proportion of the population with satisfactory knowledge of TB to 85 percent by 2019</narrative>
  </description>
